<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arnulf III, Count of Flanders</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1055–1071</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arnulf III was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> from 1070 to 1071, succeeding his father Baldwin VI as a boy under the regency of his mother Richilde. His uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-i-count-of-flanders">Robert the Frisian</a> challenged them, and Arnulf was killed at the Battle of Cassel on 22 February 1071. Robert took Flanders, while Arnulf's younger brother Baldwin kept Hainaut.</p></div>
